1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Top: the app talks to the database. Bottom: it never does.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,000
This is exactly why the top one ships. Nothing is wrong yet.

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,800
Top hands over a database password. Bottom hands over nothing.

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:10,600
Top answers him. Bottom has no address to dial.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,400
Top has no owner check to fail. Bottom filters by the token.

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,200
Top needs an app store release. Bottom is one command.

7
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,000
Not without changing the shape. That is what makes it expensive later.

8
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,800
The difference never shows up until something goes wrong.
